Reproducibility rule for a rerun diff: every PASS / FAIL / SKIP line and every
count above is reproducible byte-for-byte, because every crate is read at a
pinned published version whose bytes cannot change (crates.io releases are
immutable) and no figure here is a rolling counter. The lines that differ on
every run are the eleven carrying the $TMPDIR vendor path, which embeds the
shell's PID — the header line and the ten 'fetched ...' lines — plus the
retrieval-date line, which changes daily by construction.
